# Git's built-in `markdown` userdiff driver supplies an xfuncname, so hunk
# headers name the enclosing heading — `@@ -4,3 +4,3 @@ ## Pre-merge` instead of
# a bare line range. In a repo whose product is prose that is the difference
# between knowing which section a hunk lands in and not.
#
# What this driver does NOT supply, and why `git diff --word-diff` is a separate
# thing that needs no attribute at all, is stated once in CLAUDE.md
# § "Reading a prose diff" and pinned by scripts/test-markdown-diff-attribute.sh.
# Deliberately not restated here: that suite greps CLAUDE.md, so a second copy
# in this file would be an unpinned claim about third-party behavior sitting in
# the file that configures it — which is how a correction reaches one site and
# leaves the other asserting the opposite.
*.md diff=markdown
